SOC328 – Akira Ransomware IOCs Detected
1. Executive Summary
Severity: High
Affected Host: Vergil
IP Address: 172.16.17.130
Verdict: True Positive
Status: Endpoint isolated
Akira ransomware activity was detected after a user executed a malicious file delivered through a phishing email. Ransom notes and encrypted files confirmed ransomware impact.

2. Alert Context
Detection Source: EDR
Email Sender: sale[@]thefasted.com
Subject: Payment Confirmation
Attachment: payment-confirmation-invoice-12345.zip
Executed File: Payment Confirmation Invoice #12345.exe
Execution Path: C:\Users\LetsDefend\Downloads\payment-confirmation-invoice-12345\Payment Confirmation Invoice #12345.exe
3. Evidence Collected
File Hash (SHA-256): 2C7AEAC07CE7F03B74952E0E243BD52F2BFA60FADC92DD71A6A1FEE2D14CDD77
Ransom Note: akira_readme.txt
Encrypted File Extension: .akira
EDR Action: Detected
Variant Identification: ID Ransomware reportedly confirmed Akira.
4. Investigation
Reviewed the phishing email and confirmed the suspicious attachment.
Correlated the downloaded executable with the EDR alert.
Identified Akira ransom notes and encrypted files.
Checked email delivery scope and found one recipient.
No evidence of lateral movement was identified in the available logs.
5. Analysis and Verdict
Verdict: True Positive

The executed file, ransom notes, and .akira encrypted files support a confirmed Akira ransomware incident. The endpoint was impacted, and isolation was necessary to limit further damage.

6. MITRE ATT&CK Mapping
T1566.001 – Spearphishing Attachment: Supported.
T1486 – Data Encrypted for Impact: Supported.
T1047, T1059.001, T1059.003, T1485, T1490: Not confirmed; additional telemetry is required.
7. Response and Escalation
Action Taken: Isolated the affected endpoint from the network.

Recommended Next Steps:

Preserve forensic evidence and EDR logs.
Investigate the reported account compromise.
Hunt for related IOCs across endpoints and email systems.
Verify eradication and restore affected files from clean backups.
Confirm recovery before reconnecting the endpoint.
L2 Handoff: High-severity, True Positive Akira ransomware incident. Endpoint isolation was performed. No lateral movement was identified in the available evidence. Account compromise, potential data exfiltration, and recovery status require further investigation.
